Consider the implications of using only clean text as the deduplication key. This approach will remove legitimate repeated content that appears at different timestamps, such as recurring phrases, choruses in songs, or repeated questions in interviews. Consider adding timestamp-based logic to preserve content that appears after a significant time gap.
```suggestion
				// Use a composite key of timestamp and clean text to avoid duplicates only within the same timestamp
				compositeKey := fmt.Sprintf("%s|%s", currentTimestamp, cleanText)
				if _, exists := seenSegments[compositeKey]; !exists {
					timestampedLine := fmt.Sprintf("[%s] %s", currentTimestamp, cleanText)
					textBuilder.WriteString(timestampedLine + "\n")
					seenSegments[compositeKey] = struct{}{}
```
